{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Hand percussion kit based on the AVL Drumkits Buskman's Holiday: cajon, congas, shakers, tambourines, claves, cymbal, cowbell, foot stomp, bucket and bell tree, 21 pieces (notes 35-55, stick click on 35), 210 samples with ten velocity layers (stereo bell trees), clickable kit photo, stereo output, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Buskman's Holiday) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file for this plugin; the sample file remains under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/BuskStop-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Black Pearl 4-piece, 26 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 36-61), 118 samples with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Black Pearl) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file for this plugin; the sample file remains under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/CaptainsKit-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Automatic double tracking for vocals and other sources: four pitch-shifted, delayed copies spread across the stereo field, with high- and low-pass filters and separate dry and wet levels, ported from ADT by Christopher Arndt https://github.com/SpotlightKid/adt (MIT) JSFX version released under MIT license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Blonde Bop, played with sticks or Hot Rods (from Blonde Bop HR), 27 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 35-61, stick click on 35), 135 samples per set with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Blonde Bop) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file per set for this plugin; the sample files remain under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/Goldibops-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 DX7-style FM synthesizer, ported from Dexed by Pascal Gauthier https://github.com/asb2m10/dexed (GPLv3) Dexed's synth engine is based on Music Synthesizer for Android by Raph Levien (Google Inc.) https://github.com/google/music-synthesizer-for-android (Apache 2.0) Bundled cartridges: Dexed_01 and SynprezFM_01-32, as shipped with Dexed JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Juno-style chorus with modes I, I+II and II, tone and mix controls, ported from junologue-chorus by Peter Allwin https://github.com/peterall/junologue-chorus (MIT) JSFX version released under MIT license\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Red Zeppelin 4-piece, 26 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 36-61), 118 samples with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Red Zeppelin) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file for this plugin; the sample file remains under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/LedHead-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license\par}
}

